IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rtw-dates`
IMPORT `rtw-core`
IMPORT `rtw-seat`
IMPORT `rtw-seat-employer`

-- Return to Work Act 1986 (NT) -- cases for the employer's seat (rtw-seat-employer.l4), and MIRROR CASES: the same facts
-- asked from the worker's seat (rtw-seat.l4) and the employer's, with answers that agree.
--
-- The facts are Ana's (see rtw-cases-worker.l4), seen from her employer's side: a warehouse company insured with an
-- approved insurer, which receives her claim on Monday 9 March 2026. Average weekly earnings are ILLUSTRATIVE: $2,000.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above it.

`AWE` MEANS 2000

§ `Must I compensate this worker?`

#ASSERT `Is this person my worker under the Return to Work Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 72800 `in neither prescribed class` `AWE`
-- The owner's daughter, living at home and working in the office on PAYG, but never disclosed to the insurer: not a
-- worker (s 3B(3), (4)). Disclosed: a worker.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this person my worker under the Return to Work Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 45000 `in neither prescribed class` `AWE`)
#ASSERT `Is this person my worker under the Return to Work Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 45000 `in neither prescribed class` `AWE`
#ASSERT `Must I compensate this worker for this injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 72800 `in neither prescribed class` `the Territory` `the Territory` `the Territory` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `AWE` EQUALS `compensable under Part 5`
-- A stress claim after a performance review conducted reasonably: not an injury (s 3A(2)).
#ASSERT `Must I compensate this worker for this injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 72800 `in neither prescribed class` `the Territory` `the Territory` `the Territory` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `AWE` EQUALS `not compensable: a mental injury caused wholly or primarily by reasonable management action (s 3A(2))`

§ `How much must I pay, and until when?`

-- Week 30: as for Ana, 6750/7 dollars.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation must I pay this worker this week` 29 FALSE FALSE 1600 0 1680 600 TRUE 2 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 `AWE` EQUALS `s 65 compensation, in dollars for the week` (6750 DIVIDED BY 7)
-- In prison and maintained by the Territory: nothing (s 65A).
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation must I pay this worker this week` 29 FALSE FALSE 1600 0 1680 600 TRUE 2 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 `AWE` EQUALS `none: suspended while a prisoner (s 65A)`
#ASSERT `Until when must I pay this worker's weekly compensation` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1985) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 804 780 FALSE EQUALS `until 260 weeks have been paid, or future pension age on this day if that is earlier` (`the calendar date` 15 6 2052)
#ASSERT `What permanent impairment compensation must I pay this worker` 12 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 24960
#ASSERT `By when must I pay this worker's permanent impairment compensation` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 12 11 2026

§ `What must I do on a claim, and by when?`

#ASSERT `Where must I forward this claim` `insured with an approved insurer` EQUALS `forward the claim, and a copy, to the insurer, and keep a copy (s 84(1)(b), (c))`
#ASSERT `Where must I forward this claim` `a self-insurer` EQUALS `forward a copy of the claim to the Authority, and keep a copy (s 84(1)(a), (c))`
-- Received Monday 9 March 2026: forward by 12 March; decide by 23 March. With one weekday public holiday in the period,
-- forward by Friday 13 March.
#ASSERT `By when must I forward this claim` (`the calendar date` 9 3 2026) 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 12 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I forward this claim` (`the calendar date` 9 3 2026) 1 EQUALS `the calendar date` 13 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I decide this claim` (`the calendar date` 9 3 2026) 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 23 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I start this worker's weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 20 3 2026) 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 25 3 2026
#ASSERT `Until when does my deferral last` (`the calendar date` 20 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 15 5 2026
-- Deferred 20 March and still undecided on 16 May: deemed accepted under s 87(2).
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted this claim` (`the calendar date` 9 3 2026) 0 TRUE (`the calendar date` 20 3 2026) `defer accepting liability` FALSE (`the calendar date` 20 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 16 5 2026) EQUALS `deemed accepted under s 87(2): the deferral ran out without a decision`
-- Deferred 20 March, then disputed on 1 May without the statement, inside the deferral to 15 May: the dispute ends the
-- deferral (s 85(4)(a)), so not deemed under s 87(2).
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted this claim` (`the calendar date` 9 3 2026) 0 TRUE (`the calendar date` 20 3 2026) `defer accepting liability` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 5 2026) (`the calendar date` 16 5 2026) EQUALS `not deemed: the employer notified a decision in time`
-- Taken to have accepted, and then notifying acceptance on 27 March: until 10 April.
#ASSERT `Until when am I taken to have accepted this claim` `accept liability` (`the calendar date` 27 3 2026) EQUALS `the deemed acceptance runs until the expiry of 14 days after the notice, to` (`the calendar date` 10 4 2026)
-- A full statement with the bulletin meets s 85(8) and reg 13; without the bulletin, reg 13 is not met.
#ASSERT `Does my dispute notice meet s 85(8) and reg 13` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my dispute notice meet s 85(8) and reg 13` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `What must I do while paying, and by when?`

#ASSERT `By when must I make this weekly payment` (`the calendar date` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 22 3 2026
#ASSERT `How many weeks late was this weekly payment` (`the calendar date` 22 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 4 2026) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `By when must I give this worker earnings information` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 31 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I decide this worker's application` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 15 6 2026
#ASSERT `When does my notice of a statutory event take effect` (`the calendar date` 1 9 2026) (`the calendar date` 7 9 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 15 9 2026
-- Dismissal on 1 June for repeated refusal of reasonable instructions (serious misconduct): not an s 65C offence.
#ASSERT `Would dismissing this worker be an offence` TRUE TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not an offence under s 65C: the reason is the worker's serious misconduct (s 65C(3))`
-- An overpayment for a period ending 31 December 2025, first sought on 1 August 2026: more than 6 months before.
#ASSERT `Can I recover this overpayment` FALSE (`the calendar date` 31 12 2025) (`the calendar date` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `not recoverable unless the Court orders otherwise: it was paid for a period more than 6 months before recovery was sought (s 74(2)(b))`
-- A sole trader who misses the 21 days for earnings information: up to 17 penalty units.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `not giving earnings information within 21 days without reasonable excuse (s 85A(2))` FALSE EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `May I cut this worker's weekly compensation for not undertaking treatment` TRUE 14 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I cut this worker's weekly compensation for not undertaking treatment` TRUE 10 TRUE)

